# Cloudflare Pages: the app's pages are one single-page shell (index.html, served as "/"),
# exactly like server/web.ts APP_ROUTE. Anything else that isn't a file gets 404.html — a copy of
# the shell made by `npm run build:pages` — with a real 404, so a missing /assets/ file is never
# answered with a page. Rewrites must point at "/" (Pages redirects "/index.html" to "/").
# Exact paths first: Pages matches them faster than the splat.
/app        /  200
/app/       /  200
/pay        /  200
/pay/       /  200
/privacy    /  200
/privacy/   /  200
/terms      /  200
/terms/     /  200
/app/*      /  200
